	<h1>About</h1>
	<PageNav />

	<p>
		I'm a senior data scientist at Essentia Health. Before that I worked at NMDP and Colle McVoy.
		Before that, for quite a while, I was a political scientist.
	</p>

	<p>
		I did my graduate work at the University of Minnesota, where I studied Congress, public policy,
		and how institutions shape what governments actually manage to do. My dissertation was about
		Congress and the development of the American welfare state. I also taught political science at
		the University of Minnesota, Morris.
	</p>

	<p>
		Eventually I left academia for data science. The subject matter changed, but I never really
		stopped doing the part I liked: finding a question, figuring out what evidence would answer it,
		and usually writing some code along the way. That habit has also produced a growing pile of side
		projects, simulations, and analyses that started because I wondered about something and got
		carried away.
	</p>

	<p>
		This site is mostly a place to keep that stuff. The <a href="/blog">blog</a> has data and
		analysis write-ups; the <a href="/archive">archive</a> has the older Congress and academic-life
		material, preserved more or less as I wrote it at the time.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		The most reliable way to reach me is <a href="mailto:adam@adamolson.org"
			>adam@adamolson.org</a
		>. I'm also on <a href="https://github.com/AdamOlsonMN">GitHub</a> and
		<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adamolsonmn">LinkedIn</a>.
	</p>
</Base>
